## Undeclared Milk Allergen at Wawa Beverage Company
One of the major recalls of the week involved Wawa Beverage Company, with their lineup of bottled drinks such as Diet Lemonade and Diet Iced Tea Lemon being flagged for undeclared milk allergen. These products, though seemingly innocuous, pose a significant risk to individuals with milk allergies. The omission of milk allergen declarations is a stark reminder of the importance of detailed product labeling.

## Salmonella Concerns at Legacy Bakehouse LLC
Legacy Bakehouse LLC faced a string of recalls this week, tied to their use of potentially Salmonella-contaminated milk powder supplied by California Dairies. Products like Parmesan & Herb Bagel Crisps and Butter Parsley Bagel Crisps were affected. The ripple effects of ingredient contamination highlight the interconnectedness of food supply chains.

## Statistics: A Year Marked by Recalls
The total recalls this year stand at 509, with allergen-related incidents taking the lead at 251 cases. While allergens dominate, Salmonella, Listeria, and E. coli also make their presence known in significant numbers. Among brands, Moonlight Packing Corporation, with 11 recalls this year, holds the unenviable title of worst offender, followed closely by Ghirardelli Chocolate Company.

## What This Means for Consumers
Consumers need to stay vigilant and informed about recalls, especially those affecting widely consumed brands like Wawa and Legacy Bakehouse. Regularly checking official recall announcements and practicing good kitchen hygiene can mitigate health risks.
